  "representation": {
    "dispatch": "Existing TYPED_ARRAY_INSTALLS rows derive constructor dispatch and native/name lookup; removed twelve delegating wrappers and their three modules.",
    "ordering": "Primitive ToIndex precedes prototype lookup. Object/buffer prototype lookup precedes source and offset effects; alignment is checked before requested length coercion, which precedes detachment. Generic post-construction prototype lookup excludes TypedArray to avoid duplicate effects.",
    "realm": "Intrinsic prototype maps own per-realm TypedArray prototypes. Fixed backing allocation derives its prototype from the constructor execution realm rather than primary-realm fields; explicit buffer inputs retain their identity.",
    "copy": "Typed source initialization uses the existing validated copy operation instead of a per-element rooted JS-value list. Equal kinds preserve exact bytes; numeric content mismatch rejects even zero-length sources.",
    "roots": "Source, arguments, prototype, new target, backing and destination use existing heap roots with cleanup on normal and abrupt completion."
  },
